  "security_implications": "The default error state (illegal state_q) asserts op_ack_o = 1 together with op_fsm_err_o = 1, which could allow downstream logic (e.g., a key manager top-level FSM) to perceive a valid completion, potentially advancing through security-critical phases (key derivation, output enable) with corrupted state. If state_q is flipped by a single-event upset, the sticky error behavior may persist and repeatedly acknowledge subsequent false operations. Additionally, the unhandled cnt_i > CDIs-1 corner in StAdv can stall the advance sequence indefinitely, blocking all key generation or derivation, which is a denial-of-service vector on the key manager.",
